{"availability":"available","full":"PremDutta/genai-video-router","name":"genai-video-router","description":"Config-driven AI video model router: filter, sort, fail over, bill the quoted price. Runnable demo, tests, interactive playground.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T17:05:10Z","updated":"2026-09-25T17:05:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-video","failover","generative-ai","llm-routing","model-routing","product-management","python"],"demo":"https://premdutta.github.io/genai-video-router/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:03.185Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:03.185Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T19:01:03.185Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:21:25.558Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:40.582Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:01:03.185Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A config-driven router that picks the right AI video model for every request, fails over when a provider goes down, and never charges a user for a failure.","Generative video products don't run on one model. They run on a portfolio: a cheap self-hosted model for the free tier, a lip-sync model for dialogue scenes, a premium model for hero shots. Each one is sold by several vendors, and all of them have outages, rate limits and content filters.","This repo is a small, runnable version of the routing pattern I designed while building a generative video platform in production. No API keys needed: providers are simulated so you can see every behavior in a few seconds."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PremDutta/genai-video-router/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e398e5d4b1b911ac59cca99350168c69dd5d194b7dc007c6e16b06d0dc38f50a","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:25.863Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:21:25.863Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"wh